@startuml 06-sync-outbox
title Geonera Ingestion — 6. Sync: Outbox Worker (SyncTask drain)
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontColor #1B1B1B
skinparam ArrowColor #546E7A
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #1B1B1B
  FontSize 13

  BackgroundColor<<lock>> #EF6C00
  FontColor<<lock>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<lock>> #A34B00

  BackgroundColor<<db>> #1565C0
  FontColor<<db>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<db>> #0B3C78

  BackgroundColor<<r2>> #2E7D32
  FontColor<<r2>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<r2>> #1B5E20

  BackgroundColor<<api>> #AD1457
  FontColor<<api>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<api>> #6A0F38
}

skinparam activityDiamond {
  BackgroundColor #FFF3CD
  BorderColor #C79100
  FontColor #5D4037
}

skinparam legend {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #90A4AE
  FontColor #1B1B1B
  FontSize 12
  EntrySeparatorColor #CFD8DC
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #3E3E3E
}

legend right
  |= Tag |= Meaning |
  |<back:#EF6C00><color:#FFFFFF> lock </color></back>| Advisory-lock / Parent Handler step |
  |<back:#1565C0><color:#FFFFFF> db </color></back>| PostgreSQL transaction (state / outbox) |
  |<back:#2E7D32><color:#FFFFFF> r2 </color></back>| Cloudflare R2 storage I/O |
  |<back:#AD1457><color:#FFFFFF> api </color></back>| External Dukascopy API call |
endlegend

start
:RunSyncHandler(ctx, dal);
note right
  Triggered by queue jobs.sync (every 5 minutes).
  **NO global advisory lock** — fire & forget design.
  Concurrent triggers are allowed; no trigger is dropped.

  ** How SyncTask rows are created (publish side, NOT this process): **
  Whenever a TICK row reaches a terminal state (→ CONFIRMED,
  or CONFIRMED → BROKEN demotion) inside T-2 / Backfill-Validate,
  an "INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (instrument_id, target_date)
  DO UPDATE SET status = 'PENDING'" is executed in the SAME
  DB transaction as the status change — atomically publishing
  or resurrecting the outbox event.
end note

:**claimBatchSyncTasks** — single FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED transaction
Claim up to **12** PENDING rows:
ORDER BY hours_count DESC (nearest to 24 first), created_at ASC
→ SET status = 'PROCESSED' for each claimed row;<<db>>
note right
  hours_count tracks the last known count of
  CONFIRMED TICK rows for this instrument/day.
  Ordering DESC ensures rows close to completion
  are processed ahead of newly created ones.
  SKIP LOCKED prevents claim contention between
  concurrent triggers.
end note

if (Any PENDING tasks found?) then (none)
  :return true — nothing to do this cycle;
  stop
else (N tasks claimed, 1 ≤ N ≤ 12)
  :Launch N goroutines (fire & forget)
  RunSyncHandler returns immediately;
  note right
    Each goroutine runs processSyncTaskWorker with
    context.WithTimeout(ctx, **5 min**) + defer cancel().
    The 5-minute deadline bounds the goroutine lifetime —
    a stuck pg_advisory_xact_lock wait cannot leak forever.
    Subsequent triggers can claim more rows
    without waiting for these goroutines.
  end note
endif

' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' GOROUTINE BODY — processSyncTaskWorker (one per claimed task)
' ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

partition "processSyncTaskWorker (per goroutine)" {

  :Derive the day window:
  windowStart = task.TargetDate
  windowEnd   = windowStart + 24h;

  ' ── Step 1: count (no advisory lock needed) ──
  :COUNT(*) State
  WHERE JobType = TICK
    AND InstrumentID = task.InstrumentID
    AND Timestamp IN [windowStart, windowEnd)
    AND Status = CONFIRMED;<<db>>

  if (actualCount < 24?) then (yes — day not yet complete)
    :UPDATE ingestion.sync_tasks
    SET hours_count = actualCount,
        status = 'PENDING'
    WHERE id = task.ID;<<db>>
    note right
      Task re-queued for next trigger.
      hours_count is persisted so the next
      claim round can still prioritise this
      row correctly (ORDER BY hours_count DESC).
    end note
    stop
  else (== 24 — all hours confirmed)
    ' ── Step 2: management lock + candle finalisation ──
    :Acquire LockIDSync (1004) via Direct Connection
    pg_advisory_xact_lock — **blocking wait**
    (serialises concurrent goroutines that also
    reach count == 24 at the same time);<<lock>>
    note right
      If the lock cannot be acquired within the
      5-minute goroutine deadline, lib/pq cancels
      the blocking query via the PostgreSQL cancel
      protocol → WaitAndAcquireAdvisoryLock returns
      an error and the goroutine exits cleanly.
    end note

    :UPDATE State (CANDLE row)
    SET resolved_tick_count = 24,
        updated_at = now()
    WHERE InstrumentID = task.InstrumentID
      AND JobType = CANDLE
      AND Timestamp = windowStart;<<db>>

    :**Conditional DELETE** of the SyncTask:
    DELETE FROM ingestion.sync_tasks
    WHERE id = task.ID
      AND status = 'PROCESSED';<<db>>
    note right
      ** Lost-Update mitigation **
      If a concurrent TICK event reset the task
      to PENDING while this goroutine was running
      (publish side), the WHERE clause matches
      zero rows — the task survives for reprocessing
      on the next cycle. No event is lost.
    end note

    :Release LockIDSync
    (lockTx.Rollback() in defer);<<lock>>
    stop
  endif

}

@enduml
